md=f'''# Source map: executable composition first\n\nApplication snapshot `{SHA}`. This map records source inspection, not executed tests. Complete symbol, route, test and SQL indexes: [source-inventory.json](../validation/intake/source-inventory.json).\n\n## The executable graph\n\n`orch-server.main → loadConfig → run → NewMemoryService → controllers + API`. Startup receives flags/env/YAML configuration and a signal context. Optional `ORCH_SCHEMA_CHECK` opens PostgreSQL only for schema inspection; `migrate` is a separate main branch. Neither chooses a database-backed service. `orch-agent.main → loadConfig → NewEngineRuntimeFromEnv → WithMetrics → NewRunner.WithRuntime → Run`; its separate HTTP listener streams logs and metrics. `orch.main → cli.Execute → NewRootCommand → HTTP client → API`. `orch-loadtest` is a fourth executable, with its own memory service and synthetic state reporting, not the running network server.\n\n| Subsystem | Constructor/source | Inputs → outputs | State owner / integration |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n'''
for x in subsystems:md+=f"| {x['id']} | {link(x['constructor'])} | {x['inputs']} → {x['outputs']} | {x['state_owner']}; **{x['classification']}** |\n"
md+='''\nThe one-second scheduler is constructed, but ordinary service mutations immediately create **assigned** tasks. The independent standalone reconciler is not constructed. Leadership and autoscaling imports/constructions are absent from the server. Node monitoring is constructed; a roadmap saying it remains missing is stale. Memory mutexes protect one process, not an HA group.\n\n## Follow every field\n\n'''
for x in prop:md+=f"- **{x['stage']}**: {x['fields']}. {link(x['source'])}.\n"
md+='''\nRequests used for planning, API admission limits, and Docker cgroup enforcement are distinct contracts. Neither a valid ServiceSpec nor an adapter field establishes end-to-end propagation. The omitted resource members must remain visible in every resource/operations chapter. Job task payloads have an additional boundary: ListAssignedTasks returns only Task, so it does not synthesize the service env/auth/security envelope.\n\n## Interfaces and lifecycle\n\nConsumer interfaces include agent.Client/Runtime/HealthChecker seams, scheduler.Store/Metrics, reconciler.Store/LeaderLock/Lease, rollout dependencies, events.Store, audit.Store, image.Resolver, secrets.Envelope, GitOpsFetcher, notification SinkStore and version compatibility helpers. The complete declaration index is in JSON and links every interface to a real line. `store.Store` embeds core namespace/quota/GitOps/node/service/task/deployment/event/secret/registry stores; the separately declared JobStore, CronJobStore, VolumeStore and NotificationSinkStore are **not** embedded. Do not infer PostgreSQL implementation of these additional interfaces. Lifecycle guards live in `pkg/types/lifecycle.go`, including actual and desired task transition validation, terminal-state checks and AgentCanReportTaskStatus. Current Go types use `internal/docker`; the intended application AGENTS layout includes `internal/runtime/docker` and `internal/runtime/containerd`, which are architecture aspirations rather than current paths.\n\n## Migration pairs\n\n| Version | Source pair | Tables touched by up SQL |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n'''
for x in migrations:md+=f"| {x['id']} | [{Path(x['up']).name}]({base+x['up']}) / [{Path(x['down']).name}]({base+x['down']}) | {', '.join(x['touched_tables'])} |\n"
md+='''\nSixteen pairs do not mean sixteen executed upgrades. Schema compatibility is 15–16 and expected schema is 16, defined in `internal/version/version.go:11–18`; migration history is separately owned by schema_migrations. Initial-schema E2E coverage does not cover all later pairs.\n\n## Experiments and test prerequisites\n\nPure/seamed tests: resource and image parsing, lifecycle transitions, scheduler.Plan, reconciler with fake store, fake Docker, admission/quota arithmetic, cron matching/injected clocks, local elector, and in-memory control-plane rules. HTTP httptest and loopback health tests still open local listeners. GitOps fixtures execute `git` in temporary repositories. Real Docker tests require `ORCH_DOCKER_INTEGRATION=1`; real orchestrator Docker E2E requires `ORCH_E2E_DOCKER=1`. PostgreSQL store tests require `ORCH_INTEGRATION_DATABASE_URL`; PostgreSQL E2E requires `ORCH_E2E_DATABASE_URL`. All database URLs must refer to disposable isolated databases: tests drop/reset public schema and are unsafe on an existing cluster. Optional 1,000-service test requires `-tags=scale`. Ordinary `go test ./...` can pass while these suites skip. Inventory inspected these conditions but ran no Go tests. Actual execution records belong under validation/labs.\n\n## Inventory verification\n\nThe generator checked source paths, line bounds, 16 up/down pairs and every indexed symbol. It read all Go declarations, all test prerequisites, and the current constructor graph. No Docker, PostgreSQL or external network behavior is implied by these static checks. Next: engineering history (002).\n'''
write('editorial/SOURCE_MAP.md',md)
print('001',len(files),'Go files',len(tests),'test files',len(interfaces),'interfaces',len(routes),'routes',len(migrations),'migration pairs')
